---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="From job card to parts enquiry | Parts Relay"
  description="Prepare your first supplier enquiry, check the wording and send it through the channel your parts counter uses."
>
  <div class="lib-page lib-docs">
    <div class="lib-docwrap">
      <aside class="lib-docside">
        <nav aria-label="Guide navigation">
          <p>Quickstart</p>
          <a class="lib-current" href="/guides/guidebook/" aria-current="page">
            Prepare a supplier enquiry
          </a>
          <a href="/tools/vin-check/">Check VIN format</a>
          <a href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">Enquiry builder</a>
          <p>Reference</p>
          <a href="/guides/vehicle-identification/">Vehicle guide</a>
          <a href="/tools/part-details/">Parts guide</a>
          <a href="/tools/parts-diagrams/">Parts diagrams</a>
          <a href="/guides/counter/">Counter guide</a>
          <p>Training</p>
          <a href="/workshops/">Self-guided workshops</a>
          <a href="/library/">Resource library</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>
      <article class="lib-docbody">
        <header>
          <span class="lib-quick-label">Getting started</span>
          <h1 tabindex="-1">From job card to parts enquiry</h1>
          <p>
            Start with the technician’s diagnosis. If the job card says “left tail lamp,” ask
            whether the shop needs a bulb, a lens or the whole lamp before you call for a price.
          </p>
        </header>
        <section class="lib-doc-try">
          <h2>Prepare a note for the distributor</h2>
          <ol class="lib-steps">
            <li>
              Gather the vehicle details from the repair order. If the shop works by VIN,
              <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/tools/vin-check/">
                check its format
              </a>
              and compare it with the number on the car. A supplier will still need to confirm the
              catalogue match.
            </li>
            <li>
              Open the enquiry builder. Enter the vehicle and part, then add the quantity and any
              detail that changes the order. For a tail lamp, the side and body style can matter.
              Say whether the bulb holder has to come with it.
            </li>
            <li>
              Choose <strong>Prepare enquiry</strong> and read the brief back against the job. Use{' '}
              <strong>Edit enquiry</strong> for corrections. When it’s ready, select{' '}
              <strong>Copy enquiry</strong>, paste it into your usual email or message to the
              supplier, and send it there.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <a class="lib-action" href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">
            Prepare a parts enquiry
            <Arrow />
          </a>
        </section>
        <section class="lib-doc-try">
          <h2>When the quote comes back</h2>
          <p>
            Save the supplier’s reply with the repair order. Check the reference they priced and
            what comes with it. If the lamp and bulb holder have separate references, the estimate
            needs to account for both.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the price looks right but the fitting position is missing, ask the supplier to
            confirm the side before ordering.
            <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/tools/part-details/">
              Read a quoted reference
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="lib-doc-try">
          <h2>Questions that can hold up a request</h2>
          <div class="lib-doc-grid">
            <a href="/guides/vehicle-identification/">
              <svg
                aria-hidden="true"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.55"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              >
                <rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2" />
                <path d="M6 9v6m3-6v6m3-6v6m4-6v6m3-6v6" />
              </svg>
              <h3>The vehicle looks wrong</h3>
              <p>Find out what to compare with the job sheet before you use a catalogue result.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/tools/part-details/">
              <svg
                aria-hidden="true"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.55"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              >
                <path d="m9 3-5 6 2 8 8 4 6-5-1-8z" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" />
              </svg>
              <h3>I can’t name the piece</h3>
              <p>
                See how the counter distinguishes a single component from the assembly it belongs
                to.
              </p>
            </a>
            <a href="/repair-shops/">
              <svg
                aria-hidden="true"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.55"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              >
                <path d="M5 3h11l3 3v15H5zM8 9h8m-8 4h6m-6 4h4" />
              </svg>
              <h3>I have the technician’s notes</h3>
              <p>Use the repair shop page to decide what to pass on and which question to ask.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/guides/counter/">
              <svg
                aria-hidden="true"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.55"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              >
                <path d="M3 4h16v11H9l-6 4zm7 14h6l5 3V9" />
              </svg>
              <h3>The counter needs a closer look</h3>
              <p>
                See which details distinguish a damaged lamp housing from a bulb that needs
                replacing.
              </p>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <p class="lib-product-note">
          Parts Relay finds the parts from a plate or VIN and keeps each search in one queue the
          whole counter can see.
          <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/about/">
            How Parts Relay works
          </a>
        </p>
        <a class="lib-next" href="/workshops/first-request/">
          <span>
            <small>Workshop</small>
            <strong>Write up a job from the repair sheet</strong>
          </span>
          <Arrow />
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
